      "text": "To determine the value of \\( n \\) that makes the seven-digit number \\( 854n526 \\) divisible by 11, we use the divisibility rule for 11. According to this rule, a number is divisible by 11 if the difference between the sum of the digits in the odd positions and the sum of the digits in the even positions is a multiple of 11 (including 0).\n\nFirst, let's identify the digits and their positions:\n- The digits are \\( 8, 5, 4, n, 5, 2, 6 \\).\n- The positions are 1st, 3rd, 5th, 7th, 9th, 11th, and 13th.\n\nNext, we calculate the sum of the digits in the odd positions:\n\\[ 8 + 4 + 5 + 5 + 6 = 28. \\]\n\nNow, we calculate the sum of the digits in the even positions:\n\\[ 5 + n + 2 = 7 + n. \\]\n\nAccording to the divisibility rule, the difference between these two sums must be a multiple of 11:\n\\[ 28 - (7 + n) = 28 - 7 - n = 21 - n. \\]\nWe need \\( 21 - n \\) to be a multiple of 11. The possible values for \\( 21 - n \\) are:\n\\[ 21 - n = 0, 11. \\]\n\nSolving these equations for \\( n \\):\n1. \\( 21 - n = 0 \\)\n   \\[ n = 21 - 0 = 21 \\]\n   But \\( n \\) must be a digit (0 through 9), so \\( n = 21 \\) is not possible.\n\n2. \\( 21 - n = 11 \\)\n   \\[ n = 21 - 11 = 10. \\]\n\nThus, \\( n = 10 \\) is a possible solution. We verify this by substituting \\( n = 10 \\) back into the original number:\n\\[ 85410526. \\]\nThe sum of the digits in the odd positions is:\n\\[ 8 + 4 + 5 + 2 + 6 = 25. \\]\nThe sum of the digits in the even positions is:\n\\[ 5 + 1 + 0 + 5 + 2 = 13. \\]\nThe difference is:\n\\[ 25 - 13 = 12. \\]\nSince 12 is a multiple of 11, the number \\( 85410526 \\) is divisible by 11.\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( n \\) is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
