      "text": "To determine the value of \\( n \\) such that the seven-digit number \\( 854n526 \\) is divisible by 11, we can use the rule for divisibility by 11. The rule states that a number is divisible by 11 if the difference between the sum of the digits in the odd positions and the sum of the digits in the even positions is a multiple of 11 (including 0).\n\nLet's identify the digits and their positions:\n- The digits in the odd positions (1st, 3rd, 5th, 7th) are: \\( 8, 4, 5, 6 \\).\n- The digits in the even positions (2nd, 4th, 6th) are: \\( 5, n, 2 \\).\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of the digits in the odd positions:\n\\[\n8 + 4 + 5 + 6 = 23\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the sum of the digits in the even positions:\n\\[\n5 + n + 2 = 7 + n\n\\]\n\nAccording to the rule for divisibility by 11, the difference between these two sums must be a multiple of 11:\n\\[\n23 - (7 + n) = 16 - n\n\\]\nWe need \\( 16 - n \\) to be a multiple of 11. The possible multiples of 11 are \\( 0, \\pm 11, \\pm 22, \\ldots \\). Since \\( 16 - n \\) must be a positive multiple of 11 and \\( n \\) is a digit (0 through 9), the only feasible value is:\n\\[\n16 - n = 11\n\\]\nSolving for \\( n \\):\n\\[\nn = 16 - 11 = 5\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( n \\) that makes the number \\( 854n526 \\) divisible by 11 is \\(\\boxed{5}\\).",
