      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the value of \\( n \\) that makes the seven-digit number \\( 854n526 \\) divisible by 11, we can use the rule for divisibility by 11. The rule states that a number is divisible by 11 if the difference between the sum of the digits in the odd positions and the sum of the digits in the even positions is a multiple of 11 (including 0).\n\nFor the number \\( 854n526 \\):\n- The digits in the odd positions are \\( 8, 4, 5, \\) and \\( 6 \\).\n- The digits in the even positions are \\( 5, n, \\) and \\( 2 \\).\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of the digits in the odd positions:\n\\[ 8 + 4 + 5 + 6 = 23. \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the sum of the digits in the even positions:\n\\[ 5 + n + 2 = 7 + n. \\]\n\nAccording to the rule for divisibility by 11, the difference between these two sums must be a multiple of 11:\n\\[ 23 - (7 + n) \\equiv 0 \\pmod{11}. \\]\nSimplifying the left side, we get:\n\\[ 23 - 7 - n \\equiv 0 \\pmod{11}, \\]\n\\[ 16 - n \\equiv 0 \\pmod{11}. \\]\nThis simplifies further to:\n\\[ 16 \\equiv n \\pmod{11}. \\]\nSince \\( 16 \\div 11 = 1 \\) remainder \\( 5 \\), we have:\n\\[ n = 5. \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( n \\) is \\(\\boxed{5}\\).",
